{"surah": 88, "verses": [{"ayah": 1, "text": "هَلْ أَتَىٰكَ حَدِيثُ ٱلْغَٰشِيَةِ ", "translation": "Has there reached you the report of the Overwhelming [event]?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "هَلْ", "translit": "ْlَh", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَتَىٰكَ", "translit": "َkٰàَtَaʾ", "root": "اتي"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "حَدِيثُ", "translit": "ُhtyِdَḥ", "root": "حدث"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْغَٰشِيَةِ", "translit": "ِẗَyِhsَٰغْlٱ", "root": "غشو"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 2, "text": "وُجُوهٌ يَوْمَئِذٍ خَٰشِعَةٌ ", "translation": "[Some] faces, that Day, will be humbled,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وُجُوهٌ", "translit": "ٌhwُjgُw", "root": "وجه"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَوْمَئِذٍ", "translit": "ٍhdِyʾَmْwَy", "root": "يوم"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "خَٰشِعَةٌ", "translit": "ٌẗَʿعِhsَٰhk", "root": "خشع"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 3, "text": "عَامِلَةٌ نَّاصِبَةٌ ", "translation": "Working [hard] and exhausted.[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "عَامِلَةٌ", "translit": "ٌẗَlِmāَʿع", "root": "عمل"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "نَّاصِبَةٌ", "translit": "ٌẗَbِṣāَّn", "root": "نصب"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 4, "text": "تَصْلَىٰ نَارًا حَامِيَةً ", "translation": "They will [enter to] burn in an intensely hot Fire.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "تَصْلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlْṣَt", "root": "صلي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "نَارًا", "translit": "āًrāَn", "root": "نور"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "حَامِيَةً", "translit": "ًẗَyِmāَḥ", "root": "حمي"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 5, "text": "تُسْقَىٰ مِنْ عَيْنٍ ءَانِيَةٍ ", "translation": "They will be given drink from a boiling spring.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "تُسْقَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَqْsُt", "root": "سقي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مِنْ", "translit": "ْnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَيْنٍ", "translit": "ٍnْyَʿع", "root": "عين"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ءَانِيَةٍ", "translit": "ٍẗَyِnāَء", "root": "اني"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 6, "text": "لَّيْسَ لَهُمْ طَعَامٌ إِلَّا مِن ضَرِيعٍ ", "translation": "For them there will be no food except from a poisonous, thorny plant", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "لَّيْسَ", "translit": "َsْyَّl", "root": "ليس"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "طَعَامٌ", "translit": "ٌmāَʿعَṭ", "root": "طعم"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ضَرِيعٍ", "translit": "ٍʿعyِrَḍ", "root": "ضرع"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 7, "text": "لَّا يُسْمِنُ وَلَا يُغْنِى مِن جُوعٍ ", "translation": "Which neither nourishes nor avails against hunger.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "لَّا", "translit": "āَّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يُسْمِنُ", "translit": "ُnِmْsُy", "root": "سمن"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَلَا", "translit": "āَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "يُغْنِى", "translit": "àِnْغُy", "root": "غني"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "جُوعٍ", "translit": "ٍʿعwُjg", "root": "جوع"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 8, "text": "وُجُوهٌ يَوْمَئِذٍ نَّاعِمَةٌ ", "translation": "[Other] faces, that Day, will show pleasure.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وُجُوهٌ", "translit": "ٌhwُjgُw", "root": "وجه"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَوْمَئِذٍ", "translit": "ٍhdِyʾَmْwَy", "root": "يوم"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "نَّاعِمَةٌ", "translit": "ٌẗَmِʿعāَّn", "root": "نعم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 9, "text": "لِّسَعْيِهَا رَاضِيَةٌ ", "translation": "With their effort [they are] satisfied", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "لِّسَعْيِهَا", "translit": "āَhِyْʿعَsِّl", "root": "سعي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "رَاضِيَةٌ", "translit": "ٌẗَyِḍāَr", "root": "رضو"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 10, "text": "فِى جَنَّةٍ عَالِيَةٍ ", "translation": "In an elevated garden,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "جَنَّةٍ", "translit": "ٍẗَّnَjg", "root": "جنن"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَالِيَةٍ", "translit": "ٍẗَyِlāَʿع", "root": "علو"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 11, "text": "لَّا تَسْمَعُ فِيهَا لَٰغِيَةً ", "translation": "Wherein they will hear no unsuitable speech.[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "لَّا", "translit": "āَّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "تَسْمَعُ", "translit": "ُʿعَmْsَt", "root": "سمع"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فِيهَا", "translit": "āَhyِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَٰغِيَةً", "translit": "ًẗَyِغَٰl", "root": "لغو"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 12, "text": "فِيهَا عَيْنٌ جَارِيَةٌ ", "translation": "Within it is a flowing spring.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فِيهَا", "translit": "āَhyِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عَيْنٌ", "translit": "ٌnْyَʿع", "root": "عين"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "جَارِيَةٌ", "translit": "ٌẗَyِrāَjg", "root": "جري"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 13, "text": "فِيهَا سُرُرٌ مَّرْفُوعَةٌ ", "translation": "Within it are couches raised high", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فِيهَا", "translit": "āَhyِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "سُرُرٌ", "translit": "ٌrُrُs", "root": "سرر"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مَّرْفُوعَةٌ", "translit": "ٌẗَʿعwُfْrَّm", "root": "رفع"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 14, "text": "وَأَكْوَابٌ مَّوْضُوعَةٌ ", "translation": "And cups put in place", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَأَكْوَابٌ", "translit": "ٌbāَwْkَaʾَw", "root": "كوب"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مَّوْضُوعَةٌ", "translit": "ٌẗَʿعwُḍْwَّm", "root": "وضع"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 15, "text": "وَنَمَارِقُ مَصْفُوفَةٌ ", "translation": "And cushions lined up", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَنَمَارِقُ", "translit": "ُqِrāَmَnَw", "root": "نمرق"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مَصْفُوفَةٌ", "translit": "ٌẗَfwُfْṣَm", "root": "صفف"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 16, "text": "وَزَرَابِىُّ مَبْثُوثَةٌ ", "translation": "And carpets spread around.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَزَرَابِىُّ", "translit": "ُّàِbāَrَzَw", "root": "زرب"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مَبْثُوثَةٌ", "translit": "ٌẗَhtwُhtْbَm", "root": "بثث"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 17, "text": "أَفَلَا يَنظُرُونَ إِلَى ٱلْإِبِلِ كَيْفَ خُلِقَتْ ", "translation": "Then do they not look at the camels - how they are created?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَفَلَا", "translit": "āَlَfَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَنظُرُونَ", "translit": "َnwُrُẓnَy", "root": "نظر"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "إِلَى", "translit": "àَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْإِبِلِ", "translit": "ِlِbِiʾْlٱ", "root": "ابل"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "كَيْفَ", "translit": "َfْyَk", "root": "كيف"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "خُلِقَتْ", "translit": "ْtَqِlُhk", "root": "خلق"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 18, "text": "وَإِلَى ٱلسَّمَآءِ كَيْفَ رُفِعَتْ ", "translation": "And at the sky - how it is raised?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَإِلَى", "translit": "àَlِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلسَّمَآءِ", "translit": "ِءٓāَmَّslٱ", "root": "سمو"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "كَيْفَ", "translit": "َfْyَk", "root": "كيف"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "رُفِعَتْ", "translit": "ْtَʿعِfُr", "root": "رفع"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 19, "text": "وَإِلَى ٱلْجِبَالِ كَيْفَ نُصِبَتْ ", "translation": "And at the mountains - how they are erected?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَإِلَى", "translit": "àَlِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلْجِبَالِ", "translit": "ِlāَbِjgْlٱ", "root": "جبل"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "كَيْفَ", "translit": "َfْyَk", "root": "كيف"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "نُصِبَتْ", "translit": "ْtَbِṣُn", "root": "نصب"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 20, "text": "وَإِلَى ٱلْأَرْضِ كَيْفَ سُطِحَتْ ", "translation": "And at the earth - how it is spread out?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَإِلَى", "translit": "àَlِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلْأَرْضِ", "translit": "ِḍْrَaʾْlٱ", "root": "ارض"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "كَيْفَ", "translit": "َfْyَk", "root": "كيف"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "سُطِحَتْ", "translit": "ْtَḥِṭُs", "root": "سطح"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 21, "text": "فَذَكِّرْ إِنَّمَآ أَنتَ مُذَكِّرٌ ", "translation": "So remind, [O Muḥammad]; you are only a reminder.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَذَكِّرْ", "translit": "ْrِّkَhdَf", "root": "ذكر"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "إِنَّمَآ", "translit": "ٓāَmَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَنتَ", "translit": "َtnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مُذَكِّرٌ", "translit": "ٌrِّkَhdُm", "root": "ذكر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 22, "text": "لَّسْتَ عَلَيْهِم بِمُصَيْطِرٍ ", "translation": "You are not over them a controller.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "لَّسْتَ", "translit": "َtْsَّl", "root": "ليس"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِم", "translit": "mِhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "بِمُصَيْطِرٍ", "translit": "ٍrِṭْyَṣُmِb", "root": "سطر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 23, "text": "إِلَّا مَن تَوَلَّىٰ وَكَفَرَ ", "translation": "However, he who turns away and disbelieves –", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مَن", "translit": "nَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "تَوَلَّىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَّlَwَt", "root": "ولي"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وَكَفَرَ", "translit": "َrَfَkَw", "root": "كفر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 24, "text": "فَيُعَذِّبُهُ ٱللَّهُ ٱلْعَذَابَ ٱلْأَكْبَرَ ", "translation": "Then Allāh will punish him with the greatest punishment.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَيُعَذِّبُهُ", "translit": "ُhُbِّhdَʿعُyَf", "root": "عذب"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْعَذَابَ", "translit": "َbāَhdَʿعْlٱ", "root": "عذب"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْأَكْبَرَ", "translit": "َrَbْkَaʾْlٱ", "root": "كبر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 25, "text": "إِنَّ إِلَيْنَآ إِيَابَهُمْ ", "translation": "Indeed, to Us is their return.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "إِلَيْنَآ", "translit": "ٓāَnْyَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "إِيَابَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَbāَyِiʾ", "root": "اوب"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 26, "text": "ثُمَّ إِنَّ عَلَيْنَا حِسَابَهُم ", "translation": "Then indeed, upon Us is their account.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "ثُمَّ", "translit": "َّmُht", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَلَيْنَا", "translit": "āَnْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "حِسَابَهُم", "translit": "mُhَbāَsِḥ", "root": "حسب"}], "hasIhya": false}], "tafsir": {"4": [{"arabic": "لشوبا من حميم ثم إن مرجعهم لإلى الجحيم} وقال تعالى {تصلى نارا حامية تسقى من عين آنية} وقال تعالى {إن لدينا أنكالا وجحيما وطعاما ذا غصة وعذابا أليما} وقال ابن عباس قال رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم لو أن قطرة من الزقوم قطرت في بحار الدنيا أفسدت على أهل الدنيا معايشهم (2) فكيف من يكون طعامه ذلك وقال أنس قال رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم ارغبوا فيما رغبكم الله واحذروا وخافوا ما خوفكم اللهبه من عذابه وعقابه ومن جهنم فإنه لو كانت قطرة من الجنة معكم في دنياكم التي أنتم فيها طيبها لكم ولو كانت قطرة من النار معكم في دنياكم التي أنتم فيها خ", "english": "And ʿAlī, may God honor his face, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Seek refuge in God from the Pit of Sorrow, or the Valley of Sorrow.\" It was said: \"O Messenger of God, what is the Valley or Pit of Sorrow?\" He said: \"A valley in Hell from which Hell itself seeks refuge with God seventy times each day. God, the Exalted, has prepared it for the reciters who show off.\" (2)", "book_title": "Remembrance of Death and Afterlife", "section_title_ar": "Section 1349", "section_title_en": "The Vastness of Hellfire, Its Depths, and the Torments of Its Inhabitants", "section_index": 1349, "anchors": "- Root: و د ي (w-d-y)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: A valley; a place where torrents flow. In the lexicon, it denotes a lowland or watercourse between mountains.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Used for the valleys of Hell as places of confinement and passage, each containing further branching ravines (شُعَب), indicating graded descent.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal for earthly valleys; here transferred (majāz) to the topographical reality of Hell, affirming its corporeal vastness.\n- Root: ع م ق (ʿ-m-q)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Depth; the far bottom of a well or pit. Al-Farahidi: \"العمق: قعر البئر ونحوها.\"\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Depth as a measure of descent; in the Hereafter, it is unbounded, paralleling the unbounded depth of worldly desire.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal for physical depth; here extended to show the infinite regress of punishment corresponding to infinite craving.\n- Root: غ س ق (gh-s-q)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Stinking, foul pus or ichor that flows from the skin of the damned; also intense darkness.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Al-Ghassāq is the putrid effusion of Hell, a punishment for the senses, specifically for drinking when the damned cry out in thirst.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal for what is loathsome and fetid; in the Quranic context, it is the designated drink of the inhabitants.\n- Root: ز ق م (z-q-m)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: To swallow with difficulty; the tree of Zaqqūm, which grows in the depths of Hell.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): A specific tree in Hell whose fruit is like the heads of devils, eaten by the damned to fill their bellies, causing choking and agony.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal for a real tree; its description is sensory, not metaphorical, affirming the physical reality of punishment.\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الفصل بين الجار والمجرور (Prepositional Interposition) — The periodic structure of \"في جهنم سبعين ألف واد\" allows the prepositional phrase to precede the subject for emphasis, establishing the spatial setting before detailing its contents.", "content_type": "afterlife", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on the journey of the soul, death, and the Hereafter, from 'Remembrance of Death and Afterlife'", "badge": "Afterlife"}], "7": [{"arabic": "فيه من العذاب فيستغيثون بالطعام فيغاثون بطعام من ضريع لا يسمن ولا يغني من جوع ويستغيثون بالطعام فيغاثون بطعام ذي غصة فيذكرون كما كانوا يجيزون الغصص في الدنيا بشراب فيستغيثون بشراب فيرفع إليهم الحميم بكلاليب الحديد فإذا دنت من وجوههم شوت وجوههم فإذا دخل الشراب بطونهم قطع ما في بطونهم فيقولون ادعوا خزنة جهنم قال فيدعون خزنة جهنم أن ادعوا ربكم يخفف عنا يوما من العذاب فيقولون أو لم تك تأتيكم رسلكم بالبينات قالوا بلى قالوا فادعوا وما دعاء الكافرين إلا في ضلال قال فيقولون ادعوا مالكا فيدعون فيقولون يا مالك ليقض علينا ربك قال فيجي", "english": "And ʿAlī, may God honor his face, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Seek refuge in God from the Pit of Sorrow, or the Valley of Sorrow.\" It was said: \"O Messenger of God, what is the Valley or Pit of Sorrow?\" He said: \"A valley in Hell from which Hell itself seeks refuge with God seventy times each day. God, the Exalted, has prepared it for the reciters who show off.\" (2)", "book_title": "Remembrance of Death and Afterlife", "section_title_ar": "Section 1349", "section_title_en": "The Vastness of Hellfire, Its Depths, and the Torments of Its Inhabitants", "section_index": 1349, "anchors": "- Root: و د ي (w-d-y)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: A valley; a place where torrents flow. In the lexicon, it denotes a lowland or watercourse between mountains.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Used for the valleys of Hell as places of confinement and passage, each containing further branching ravines (شُعَب), indicating graded descent.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal for earthly valleys; here transferred (majāz) to the topographical reality of Hell, affirming its corporeal vastness.\n- Root: ع م ق (ʿ-m-q)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Depth; the far bottom of a well or pit. Al-Farahidi: \"العمق: قعر البئر ونحوها.\"\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Depth as a measure of descent; in the Hereafter, it is unbounded, paralleling the unbounded depth of worldly desire.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal for physical depth; here extended to show the infinite regress of punishment corresponding to infinite craving.\n- Root: غ س ق (gh-s-q)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Stinking, foul pus or ichor that flows from the skin of the damned; also intense darkness.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Al-Ghassāq is the putrid effusion of Hell, a punishment for the senses, specifically for drinking when the damned cry out in thirst.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal for what is loathsome and fetid; in the Quranic context, it is the designated drink of the inhabitants.\n- Root: ز ق م (z-q-m)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: To swallow with difficulty; the tree of Zaqqūm, which grows in the depths of Hell.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): A specific tree in Hell whose fruit is like the heads of devils, eaten by the damned to fill their bellies, causing choking and agony.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal for a real tree; its description is sensory, not metaphorical, affirming the physical reality of punishment.\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الفصل بين الجار والمجرور (Prepositional Interposition) — The periodic structure of \"في جهنم سبعين ألف واد\" allows the prepositional phrase to precede the subject for emphasis, establishing the spatial setting before detailing its contents.", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Remembrance of Death and Afterlife'", "badge": "Insight"}], "14": [{"arabic": "أن يذهب بصره ثم يطأطىء رأسه فإذا أزواجه وأكواب موضوعة ونمارق مصفوفة وزرابي مبثوثة ثم اتكأ فقال الحمد لله الذي هدانا لهذا وما كنا لنهتدي", "english": "...of death, hunger, thirst, and all other kinds of calamities, he would be worthy of abandoning this world because of them, and of not preferring it over that whose cutting-off and vexation are of its very necessity. How [could he prefer it], when its people — the kings — are secure, and in varieties of joy are delighting? For them therein is all they desire, and every day they attend at the courtyard of the Throne, and gaze upon the noble Face of Allah. They attain, through that gazing upon Allah, that which makes them not look, along with it, at the rest of the delights of the Gardens, nor do they turn aside. They are perpetually moving among these kinds of blessings, and they are secure from their passing away. Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \"A herald will call out: 'O People of Paradise! Verily for you is that you be healthy and never be ill; and for you is that you live and never die; and for you is that you be young and never grow old; and for you is that you be in bliss and never suffer misery.'\" That is the saying of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: {«And they will be called: 'This is the Paradise which you have been made to inherit for what you used to do'»} (7:43).", "book_title": "Remembrance of Death and Afterlife", "section_title_ar": "Section 1352", "section_title_en": "The Description of Paradise: Its Gates, Rivers, and the Bliss of Its Inhabitants", "section_index": 1352, "anchors": "- Root: نعم (n-'-m)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core root denotes ease, comfort, and the state of well-being; al-Ayn notes it is also a name for the leopard and panther, indicating swiftness and grace.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"النعمة: الحالة الحسنة\" — the goodly state; \"النعيم\" is the enduring, perfect form of bliss, specifically tied to divine reward in the afterlife.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (Haqiqah): \"نعم عيشه\" — a life of ease and pleasantness. Metaphorical (Majaz): \"خفّت نعامتهم\" — their prosperity departed, showing the root's extension to transient worldly goods, contrasted here with eternal Paradise.\n- Root: اهل (a-h-l)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core root signifies those united by kinship, dwelling, or faith; al-Ayn notes it also refers to the prominent part of a beast's back, implying a place of honor and rest.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"أهل الرجل: من يجمعه وإياهم نسب أو دين\" — the people of a man are those joined by lineage or religion; \"أهل الجنة\" (the People of Paradise) are thus bound by the covenant of faith and divine favor.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"رجعوا إلى أهاليهم\" — returning to one's family. Here, the \"أهل الجنة\" are the inhabitants of Paradise, addressed by the herald as a household of eternal blessedness.\n- Root: باب (b-a-b)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core root denotes a door or gateway; al-Ayn links it to \"إبهام\" (obscurity/concealment), as a door hides what lies within until opened.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الباب\" is the means of access to a thing; in the Quranic context, the gates of Paradise are the entry points to divine mercy, each corresponding to a specific act of obedience.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: physical gates of a city or house. Metaphorical: \"أبواب الجنة\" are the spiritual avenues of righteous deeds (prayer, fasting, charity, jihad) through which the believer enters divine reward.\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الفصل بين الجار والمجرور (Prepositional Interposition) — The rule permits separation between a preposition and its governed noun for rhetorical emphasis, as seen in \"لهم فيها كل ما يشتهون\" (for them therein is all they desire), where \"لهم\" is fronted for exclusivity and \"فيها\" interposed to stress the locus of bliss.", "content_type": "dua", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on supplications, prayers, and their spiritual power, from 'Remembrance of Death and Afterlife'", "badge": "Du'a"}]}, "wordTiming": {"abdulbasit": {"1": [[1, 350, 688], [2, 688, 1684], [3, 1684, 2520], [4, 2520, 3685]], "2": [[1, 350, 1607], [2, 1607, 3249], [3, 3249, 4521]], "3": [[1, 250, 1652], [2, 1652, 3443]], "4": [[1, 250, 1318], [2, 1318, 2292], [3, 2292, 3417]], "5": [[1, 350, 1462], [2, 1462, 1852], [3, 1852, 2574], [4, 2574, 3685]], "6": [[1, 350, 1328], [2, 1328, 1980], [3, 1980, 3126], [4, 3126, 4149], [5, 4149, 4599], [6, 4599, 5722]], "7": [[1, 350, 1057], [2, 1057, 2028], [3, 2028, 2894], [4, 2894, 3971], [5, 3971, 4393], [6, 4393, 5174]], "8": [[1, 350, 1596], [2, 1596, 3224], [3, 3224, 5017]], "9": [[1, 250, 1774], [2, 1774, 2947]], "10": [[1, 350, 968], [2, 968, 2019], [3, 2019, 3528]], "11": [[1, 350, 1008], [2, 1008, 1852], [3, 1852, 2834], [4, 